# Bayesian Analysis in Applications of Hierarchical Models: Issues and Methods.

**Authors:** Seltzer, Michael H., And Others

## Abstract
The Gibbs sampling algorithms presented by M. H. Seltzer (1993) are fully generalized to a broad range of settings in which vectors of random regression parameters in the hierarchical model are assumed multivariate normally or multivariate &quot;t&quot; distributed across groups. The use of a fully Bayesian approach is discussed. (SLD)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ531743

